=== CONFIRMED: a commanded power-off was LOST by the twin ===
  s5 and s6 both: manifest pid null, gRPC port closed, 8 bmv2 processes. Both commanded off
  through the same endpoint 45 s apart, both returned Success.
    s5 -> is_up=False, power_state=OFF   (correct)
    s6 -> is_up=True,  power_state=ON    (WRONG), stable across 3 samples 5 s apart, ~3 min later.
  The proxy is not the cause: it lists neither 5 nor 6 in /v1.0/topology/switches any more and
  reports probe_ok=False / stream_alive=False for both. The wrong value is simply stuck, and by
  D15 nothing in the system will ever correct it.
  Score so far: 1 lost out of 3 commanded power-offs tonight (s7 ok, s5 ok, s6 lost) => a race.

